<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns &quot;AA-&quot; rating to KEPCO bonds.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns &quot;AA-&quot; rating to KEPCO bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard and Poor's (S&amp;P) said on Tuesday that it had assigned its AA- rating to Korea Electric Power Corp's (KEPCO) 150 million sterling 8.5 percent straight bonds due on April 28, 2007. It said the rating reflected the company's strong ties with the South Korean government, its strong operational and financial profiles, and a favourable regulatory regime.</p>
<p>The outlook for the rating was stable, S&amp;P said.</p>
</text>
